WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.107 --> 00:00:06.689
AppShelf sells hosted WordPress sites for nine dollars a month, billed with Stripe.

2
00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:08.967
Pick one of three starter templates.

3
00:00:09.117 --> 00:00:12.648
Sign up in seconds. There's no email check in this demo.

4
00:00:12.798 --> 00:00:15.872
Choose a template, name the site, and pick a free address.

5
00:00:16.022 --> 00:00:20.429
Then pay on Stripe Checkout, in test mode, with Stripe's own test card number.

6
00:00:20.579 --> 00:00:24.014
Stripe sends a webhook, and a worker builds the WordPress site.

7
00:00:24.164 --> 00:00:26.072
And just like that, it's live.

8
00:00:26.222 --> 00:00:28.907
Here's the new restaurant site, ready to edit.

9
00:00:29.057 --> 00:00:32.685
Cancel the plan, and the licence turns inactive right away.

10
00:00:32.885 --> 00:00:35.948
Visitors now see a notice that the site is archived.

11
00:00:36.098 --> 00:00:39.855
Renew it from the dashboard, and pay again with the same test card.

12
00:00:40.005 --> 00:00:42.220
Seconds later, it's back online.

13
00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.343
Same site, same content.

14
00:00:44.743 --> 00:00:48.313
Built with Next.js, Postgres, Stripe and WordPress.
